{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,200p' docs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Core 0.1 debt source lowering, version 1\n\nThis executable profile supplements the protected Core 0 grammar and contract.\n`compile_source(text, bindings)` parses real source; `compile_program(Program,\nbindings)` accepts immutable typed declarations. Both bind names, check quantities\nand context, construct shared IR, and submit it to independent schema and semantic\nvalidation. Neither entrypoint reads the authored expected IR or expected results.\n\n## Repair execution audit\n\nThe approved P03 plan remains the implementation boundary. Inspection of the\ntimed-out attempt found two partial modules and no tests or deliverables. Its\nsuccessful example compile was insufficient: global constraints were dropped,\nrates were treated as dimensionless, and acceptance, package and domain checks\nwere incomplete. These are implementation failures, not evidence against the\nlanguage design. Repair them before accepting the slice.\n\nThe baseline is `borrowing.acc`, plus documented corresponding fields of the\nauthored IR, whose reconstruction claims are excluded. Independently constructed\ntyped programs and exact arithmetic checks supplement agreement between frontends.\nSchema validity is a prerequisite, not semantic acceptance. Negative IR cases must\nbe structurally valid before testing the intended semantic rejection. Stops are\nunexpected protected-input changes, missing dependencies, or failing mandatory\nchecks; failures trigger repair, never a passing report. No statistical, timing,\nusability, accounting-compliance or forecasting comparison is being run.\n\nProvenance of material choices: exact rationals, lexical rules and quantities come\nfrom `core-contract.md`; USD accounts and DebtMix fields come from the local\nDemoDebt package. These are bounded baseline restrictions, not promoted defaults.\nThe single source/observation/symbol restriction keeps the evidence view explicit;\nmultiple-source reconciliation is unsupported. Synthetic acceptance and admission\nrecords are supplied by the caller. Absence of reconstruction requires Unknown\nfeasibility, PartialSearch, zero completed cells, one unsearched cell, no witnesses\nand no solver results. Early diagnostics cover unit loss, silent constraint loss,\ninvented acceptance and copied package digests. A pass establishes deterministic\nengineering conformance only. Results are preserved in the two P03 deliverables.\n\nThe writable project files are the two versioned modules, checker, required test,\nthis profile, the versioned cases JSON and the two P03 deliverables. Existing\ngrammar/schema, authored fixtures, legacy validators, controllers, release-pinned\nfiles and preserved snapshots remain protected. Their current hashes are checked\nagainst phase-entry hashes where available, and before/after execution. Git is\nunavailable (existing marker is not a usable repository); no Git initialization.\nPython 3.11.15, Lark 1.3.1 and jsonschema 4.26.0 are existing dependencies. No\naccelerator framework, service, installation, model or background job is used.\n\n## Supported language and bindings\n\nThe profile has one module, DemoDebt@1 import, source, entity, USD book, exact\ninstant debt observation, admitted Real interval symbol, opening, DebtMix\ncontract, constant annual-rate stress and package report. Its four account names\nare Cash, Debt, InterestExpense and Retained, with Asset, Liability, Expense and\nEquity roles respectively: the package report actually names these accounts.\nOther declaration names may vary. There may be multiple lets, Boolean constraints\nand conditional alternatives, with multiple assumptions in each alternative.\nGlobal constraints constrain the parent family; alternative constraints stay in\ntheir respective branches and are not conjoined in the parent. No branch is\nselected or solved.\n\nBindings explicitly supply a digest-locked local package, synthetic reading and\nacceptance action, information/system cutoffs, opening balances, perimeter,\nsymbol admission, assumption periods/origins, and alternative authorship. Binding\nrecords remain separate from package definitions. Every acceptance must explicitly\nsay Accept; no declaration creates acceptance. Package loading is restricted to\nthe retained DemoDebt file and checks its fixed version, digest, exports and\napplicability. Paths escaping the repository and overrides are errors. The\npackage's registry examples and expected-result fields are not compiler inputs.\n\nDecimal tokens become Fraction directly; binary floats are rejected. Strings use\nJSON escapes, reject unpaired surrogates and normalize semantic strings to NFC.\nOriginal spelling and Unicode-code-point offsets remain in the separate source\nmap; typed locations identify constructors. LF, CRLF, comments and whitespace\npreserve semantics. Dates are Gregorian. All grammar words are reserved.\n\nExpressions include literals, shared references, `value(observation)`, unary minus,\n`not`, compatible addition/subtraction, numeric comparisons, typed equality and\nBoolean composition. Multiplication admits a dimensionless Real or Int factor;\ndivision requires a provably nonzero constant Real or Int denominator. Rates and\nYearFraction are dimensional; rate times money is rejected here (the general\n`simpleInterest` builtin is future work). Integer products remain integer; division\nof scalars returns Real. Addition and comparisons require equal types and compatible\ncontexts. `constant(rate)` is a scenario driver, with a constant, nonnegative annual\nrate. `external(string)` is admitted only for source/opening/report declarations.\nDebtMix principal must equal the accepted debt and opening liability, its fraction\nmust have proven bounds inside [0,1], and component rates must be constant and\nnonnegative. Interval arithmetic proves only conservative bounds; failure to prove\na bound rejects this profile and does not assert mathematical infeasibility.\n\n## Verification and remaining coverage\n\nRun `python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_accounting_p03.py' -v`, then\n`python3 -B scripts/check_accounting_p03.py --output-dir data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03`.\nThe checker returns nonzero for failed or skipped obligations, includes generated\nIR and binding projections, observations, diagnostics, hashes and runtime details,\nand writes only conformance.json and result.md under the declared output folder.\n\nThe semantic comparison retains IR values, contexts, locks, evidence, assumptions\nand all external bindings. It excludes frontend offsets and observation display\nspelling; those are separately preserved. The authored comparison uses debt value,\ncontext, contract types/fields, assumptions, endpoint conditions, scenario rate,\nopening balances and report policies. Exact one-year interest is checked as\nP * (alpha * fixed_rate + (1-alpha) * stress_rate), using evaluated generated\nfields. At alpha=1/0, P=100 and 5%/7% imply 5/7; 9% stress implies 5/9;\nP=200 implies 10/14. This calculation is not journal execution or forecasting.\n\nMC02/MC04 receive bounded context, evidence and assumption preservation checks;\nMC10 receives factual admission and explicit scenario-assumption checks; MC20\nreceives locked-package and override rejection checks; MC23 receives matched\ntyped/text tasks; MC24 receives parsing, binding, typing and semantic diagnostics.\nNone is wholly closed by this profile. G2, G12 and G15 remain open, as do all wider\nMC01–MC35 and G1–G18 obligations.\n\nUnsupported: general package loading, events, rules/overrides, postings, arbitrary\nreport mappings, records/arrays/field access, finite choices, nonlinear bound\nproofs, implicit conversions, multiple books/entities/observations, dimensions,\ncurrency/calendar variants, rounded or period observations, source conflicts and\nrevisions, cross-company mapping, extraction uncertainty, accounting elections,\nmeasurement estimates, behavior policies, future innovations and probability\nmeasures. Reconstruction, accounting execution, forecast validity, authoring\nsuperiority and human acceptance require separate evidence.\n\n## Current execution evidence contract\n\nThe refreshed approved plan passed skeptical review. Baselines, acceptance and\nstops remain those above; historical controller/P02 changes predate this worker\nand are not worker edits. A snapshot of 370 existing phase-entry files was taken.\nMandatory case coverage is enforced by the checker against the versioned catalog.\nThe paired typed programs are constructed independently of parsing and expected IR.\nMaterial metadata (calendar, horizon, perimeter and uncertainty kind) must be\nexplicit outside the named synthetic demo helper. Their provenance is caller\nevidence, their purpose is reproducible context, their failure mode is silent\ncontext transfer, and omission/renaming tests are the earliest diagnostic. They\nare inputs, not promoted defaults. Exact arithmetic and schema validation are\nengineering diagnostics only. No stochastic or research ranking is undertaken.\n\n## Recovery integrity repair\n\nA fresh nine-method suite passed, but focused schema-valid omission probes found\nthat all assumptions or the report could be removed without rejection. These\nwere validator defects. Mandatory profile cardinalities and model/package/scope\nreferences now undergo independent checks. Every global or branch condition and\nevery assumed rate must retain matching assumption metadata; renaming an\nassumption cannot bypass its binding. Scenario driver names and scope calendars\nare checked. Ten additional schema-valid corruptions test these repairs. The\nchecker also rejects duplicate obligation IDs and explicitly failed observations.\nProtected-input hashes captured at repair entry are embedded in conformance.json.\nThese repairs strengthen bounded engineering evidence without broadening the\nprofile or establishing accounting or forecast validity.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,230p' scripts/check_accounting_p03.py\"","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Execute all catalogued P03 obligations and preserve actual observations.\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nimport hashlib\nimport io\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport platform\nimport sys\nimport time\nimport unittest\nfrom importlib.metadata import version\n\nROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nsys.path.insert(0,str(ROOT/'tests'))\nimport test_accounting_p03 as cases\n\nCHANGED=['scripts/core0_frontends_v1.py','scripts/core0_ir_v1.py','scripts/check_accounting_p03.py',\n         'tests/test_accounting_p03.py','docs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md',\n         'docs/design/fixtures/p03-lowering-cases-v1.json']\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser=argparse.ArgumentParser();parser.add_argument('--output-dir',required=True);args=parser.parse_args()\n    out=Path(args.output_dir).resolve()\n    if out != ROOT/'data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03':\n        parser.error('output-dir must be the declared P03 output directory')\n    started=time.monotonic()\n    entry=json.loads((ROOT/'data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P03/phase-entry-inventory.json').read_text())\n    before={p:hashlib.sha256((ROOT/p).read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in entry if (ROOT/p).is_file()}\n    cases.OBSERVATIONS.clear(); stream=io.StringIO()\n    suite=unittest.defaultTestLoader.loadTestsFromModule(cases)\n    result=unittest.TextTestRunner(stream=stream,verbosity=0).run(suite)\n    catalog=json.loads((ROOT/'docs/design/fixtures/p03-lowering-cases-v1.json').read_text())\n    required_counts=Counter(c['id'] for c in catalog['obligations'])\n    observed_counts=Counter(c['id'] for c in cases.OBSERVATIONS)\n    required=set(required_counts)\n    observed=set(observed_counts)\n    duplicate_ids=sorted(k for k in required|observed if required_counts[k]>1 or observed_counts[k]>1)\n    failed_observations=[c['id'] for c in cases.OBSERVATIONS if c.get('passed') is not True]\n    missing=sorted(required-observed);extra=sorted(observed-required)\n    after={p:hashlib.sha256((ROOT/p).read_bytes()).hexdigest() if (ROOT/p).is_file() else None for p in before}\n    protection=[p for p in before if before[p]!=after[p]]\n    initial=Path('/tmp/accdsl-p03-protected-entry.json')\n    worker_changes=[]\n    if initial.exists():\n        worker_changes=[p for p,h in json.loads(initial.read_text()).items() if not (ROOT/p).is_file() or hashlib.sha256((ROOT/p).read_bytes()).hexdigest()!=h]\n    repair_entry=Path('/tmp/accdsl-p03-repair-entry.json')\n    repair_before=json.loads(repair_entry.read_text()) if repair_entry.exists() else {}\n    repair_changes=[p for p,h in repair_before.items() if not (ROOT/p).is_file() or hashlib.sha256((ROOT/p).read_bytes()).hexdigest()!=h]\n    passed=(result.wasSuccessful() and result.testsRun>0 and not result.skipped and not missing and not extra\n            and not duplicate_ids and not failed_observations and not protection and not worker_changes and not repair_changes)\n    payload={\n      'schema_version':'accdsl.p03.conformance.v1','passed':passed,'profile':catalog['profile'],\n      'manifest':{'git_commit':'unavailable: existing marker is not a usable repository',\n        'command':'python3 -B scripts/check_accounting_p03.py --output-dir data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03',\n        'environment':{'python':platform.python_version(),'lark':version('lark'),'jsonschema':version('jsonschema')},\n        'hardware':'CPU only; no accelerator framework imported','random_seeds':'N/A: deterministic checks',\n        'data_version':'synthetic P03 bindings and digest-locked DemoDebt@1',\n        'utc':datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),'wall_seconds':round(time.monotonic()-started,3),\n        'plan':'data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T205123-6b8e9a16/P03/approved-plan.json',\n        'result':'data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03/result.md',\n        'outputs':['data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03/conformance.json','data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03/result.md'],\n        'changed_files':CHANGED+['data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03/'+n for n in ('conformance.json','result.md','progress.md')]},\n      'tests':{'methods_run':result.testsRun,'obligations_run':len(observed),'missing':missing,'uncatalogued':extra,\n               'duplicate_ids':duplicate_ids,'failed_observations':failed_observations,\n               'skipped':result.skipped,'failures':[{'test':str(t),'detail':d} for t,d in result.failures+result.errors]},\n      'observations':cases.OBSERVATIONS,\n      'hashes':{p:hashlib.sha256((ROOT/p).read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in CHANGED},\n      'protected_files':{'before':before,'after':after,'changed_during_check':protection,\n          'repair_entry':repair_before,'changed_during_repair':repair_changes,\n          'changed_during_worker':worker_changes,'historical_differences':[p for p in before if before[p]!=entry[p]]},\n      'requirement_coverage':{'MC02':'context and provenance','MC04':'separate alternatives and global constraints',\n         'MC10':'explicit historical admission and scenario assumptions','MC20':'package digest/applicability and report policies',\n         'MC23':'independent matched typed/text programs; no authoring superiority claim','MC24':'bounded parsing, binding, typing and independent IR rejection'},\n      'unsupported':catalog['unsupported'],\n      'acceptance':{'engineering':passed,'accounting_validity':'not established','forecast_validity':'not established',\n                    'human_acceptance':'pending','whole_gap_closure':False}}\n    out.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\n    (out/'conformance.json').write_text(json.dumps(payload,indent=2,ensure_ascii=True)+'\\n')\n    decision='PASS' if passed else 'FAIL'\n    (out/'result.md').write_text(f'''# P03 bounded source lowering result\n\n{decision}: {result.testsRun} unittest methods executed {len(observed)} catalogued obligations.\nThe compiler parses source declarations, binds explicit package/evidence/context\nmetadata, checks quantities, and constructs independently validated shared IR.\nDirect typed declarations use the same semantic stages. Neither compiler entrypoint\nreads expected IR. Complete actual IR, bindings, source spans, raw hashes and exact\nexpected/observed interest values are retained in conformance.json.\n\nIndependent renamed input and principal/rate changes establish input sensitivity.\nBaseline endpoint interest is 5/7; 9% stress gives 5/9; principal 200 gives 10/14.\nThese are exact one-year arithmetic checks, not journal execution. The authored IR\ncomparison covers corresponding economic/context/policy fields and excludes its\nreconstruction claims. Schema-valid corruptions must fail semantic validation.\n\nRecovery inspection found that removing all assumption metadata or the report\nmapping could pass the previous semantic validator. The repair rejects these\nomissions, disconnected model/package/scope references, missing scenario drivers\nand metadata changes hidden by renamed assumption identifiers. Added catalogued\nregressions first establish unchanged-schema validity, then semantic rejection.\n\n| Decision | Primary criterion | Veto diagnostics | Main uncertainty | Next action | Not concluded |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {decision} for bounded engineering conformance | independent frontends, changed inputs and rejection coverage | missing obligations={len(missing)}, failures={len(result.failures)+len(result.errors)}, protected changes={len(protection)+len(worker_changes)+len(repair_changes)} | unimplemented language breadth and domain acceptance | independent result review | whole G2/G12/G15 closure, accounting or forecasting validity |\n\nSpecification is the versioned profile. Implemented behavior is in the two versioned\nmodules. Tested invariants are the executed catalog obligations. Accounting validity,\nempirical forecasting and human acceptance remain separate and unestablished.\nAll MC01–MC35 and G1–G18 retain wider obligations.\n\nThe strongest alternative explanation for frontend agreement is a shared compiler\nbug; independent arithmetic, authored-field comparison and schema-valid corruptions\nreduce that risk without proving the general language. The weakest evidence is\ncoverage outside this debt profile. A counterexample within the declared profile\nwould overturn this engineering acceptance and trigger a focused repair.\n\nActual checker command: `{payload['manifest']['command']}`.\nEnvironment: Python {platform.python_version()}, Lark {version('lark')}, jsonschema\n{version('jsonschema')}; deterministic CPU execution, no random seed or GPU use.\nWall time: {payload['manifest']['wall_seconds']} seconds. Git commit unavailable;\nsource and protected-input hashes are in conformance.json. No package installation.\nThe standalone required unittest command was also run; its final outcome is recorded\nin progress.md. Changed code, tests and profile/catalog files are enumerated in the\nmanifest. Historical controller/P02 changes predate this worker.\n\nResiduals: general packages, events, rules, postings, arbitrary mappings, multiple\nentities/books/observations, currencies/calendars, cross-company concepts, extraction\nuncertainty, accounting elections, estimates, behavior, future innovations and\nprobability measures remain unsupported. Families remain Unknown/PartialSearch with\nzero completed cells, one unsearched cell and no invented witnesses or solver results.\n''')\n    print(json.dumps({'passed':passed,'methods':result.testsRun,'obligations':len(observed),'missing':missing,\n          'failures':len(result.failures)+len(result.errors),'protected_changes':protection+worker_changes+repair_changes}))\n    return 0 if passed else 1\n\nif __name__=='__main__':sys.exit(main())\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
